// `staff` — read staff notation, and produce a `std::notation::staff` document.
//
// A region of this adapter is a page of staff notation written in text. It
// expands to one ordinary expression — a call to the staff package's
// `Document` constructor — which is then resolved, checked, and evaluated
// exactly as if the composer had written it out. The adapter reads; the
// package decides. Nothing here computes a sounding pitch, a performed
// duration, an exact tuplet span, or a grace note's timing: those are
// `realize`'s and a performance profile's answers, and an adapter that
// pre-computed them would be deciding at read time what the package defers.
//
// # The spelling
//
//     syntax staff {
//         instrument "bb_clarinet"
//         transposing M2
//         clef treble
//         key d major
//         time (4, 4)
//         spelling shortest_readable
//
//         pickup (1, 4) { g4/4 }
//
//         repeat (2) {
//             bar (4, 4) { c5/4 d5/4. e5/8 f5/4 ~ }
//             bar (4, 4) { f5/8 rest/8 [g4 b4 d5]/4 c5(3/8) rest/8 }
//
//             ending (1) {
//                 bar (4, 4) { slur { tuplet (3, 2) { a4/8 b4/8 c5/8 } d5/4 } grace [e5] f5/2 }
//             }
//
//             ending (2) {
//                 meter (3, 4)
//                 bar (3, 4) { g5/4 a5/4 b5/4 }
//             }
//         }
//     }
//
// One rule covers every form in it: a **word**, then its **parentheses** if it
// takes numbers, then its **braces** if it holds notation. `bar (4, 4) { … }`,
// `tuplet (3, 2) { … }` and `repeat (2) { … }` are the same shape, and
// `slur { … }` is that shape with the numbers left off. A chord and a grace
// hold pitches rather than notation, so they take brackets instead of braces:
// `[g4 b4 d5]/4` and `grace [e5]`.
//
// # Why it is not the layout a musician would draw
//
// The compiler hands an adapter the fixed lexer's tokens grouped by matched
// delimiters and nothing else. There are no lines: `Whitespace` is one
// undifferentiated trivia kind, and a newline is not a token an adapter can
// see. So a spelling that meant one thing per line could not be read at all,
// and the forms are delimited instead. That is the one place this notation
// departs from what the trial note drew, and it is the compiler's shape
// showing through rather than a preference.
//
// `time (4, 4)` is two numbers rather than `4/4` for the same kind of reason:
// the lexer keeps `4/4` whole as one rational token, and a rational is
// reduced, so `4/4` and `1/1` arrive identical. A time signature is a count of
// a unit and not a quotient, so the two numbers are written as two.
//
// # `time` opens a staff and `meter` changes one
//
// A page states `time (4, 4)` at its head, and a change of meter part-way
// through states `meter (3, 4)` where it happens. They are two words because
// there are no lines: a word written above the music and the same word written
// among it arrive here identically, so a single spelling would leave the reader
// guessing which of the two the composer meant — and guessing wrong turns a
// change of meter into a second opening statement, or the reverse. Two words
// is one more thing to learn and nothing left to infer.
//
// # Every bar states what it measures
//
// `bar (4, 4) { … }` says its own meter, and its contents are checked against
// it. Nothing is inherited: the same reason a note states its own octave and
// its own written value is the reason a bar states its own length. A reader
// looking at one bar can say whether it is full without looking anywhere else,
// and so can this adapter — which is what lets the check land on the bar the
// composer wrote rather than on the page.
//
// It is also what the compiler's shape asks for. The fold runs from the leaves
// up, so a bar is read before anything enclosing it has been read; a meter
// arriving from an enclosing form would have to travel the other way, and the
// only way to carry it would be to fold every node to a function of a reader
// state. The notation says the meter twice instead, and stays readable.
//
// `pickup (1, 4) { … }` is a bar of a stated length that is not the meter, and
// it produces a `Bar` like any other: the package has no pickup, because a
// pickup is a bar with fewer beats in it.
//
// # What this adapter wanted and did not get
//
// - **A number it computed cannot be written back as a numeral.** Every number
//   this adapter emits is a token the composer wrote, echoed. That is why dots
//   are counted through a four-valued `Dots` rather than a `Nat`: `NoteValue`
//   takes a count, and the only way to hand it one is to spell it. Four dots
//   are refused for the same reason, and closing that would take an operation
//   turning a phase number into a literal token.
// - **A list cannot be built.** A group's children arrive as a `List` and
//   there is no way to add one to it. Reading them into right-nested data no
//   longer needs a closure: prompt 127dcfaa gave `list` a fold that runs from
//   its end, which is what `read_body` uses.
// - **A tie's continuation is checked by spelling, not by pitch.** There is no
//   operation reading a pitch out of a token, so `f5` tied to `f#5` is caught
//   by comparing the two spellings the composer wrote. That is the check §2.5
//   of the trial note asks for, and it is also all this adapter can see.
// - **A region is reformatted generically until this adapter can print one.**
//   `readable` means no `print`, so `musa format` reflows a region by the
//   compiler's own rules, and the blank lines a page was laid out with do not
//   survive it. Prompt 127dcfb's `print` is what closes this, and until then a
//   staff page is spaced the way the formatter spaces expressions.
// - **A refusal cannot quote the numbers it computed.** "This bar does not hold
//   what it says it measures" points at the bar and stops there; saying *by how
//   much* would mean spelling a computed rational back as text, which is the
//   first item on this list again. The place is the half that matters — the
//   package could find the same fault and could not point anywhere — but the
//   sentence is poorer than the trial note drew it.

library {
    // Read-only, of the three levels: prompt 127dcfb gives this adapter `edit`
    // and `print`, and until it does, a region of this adapter is source a
    // musician changes by typing.
    let level = "readable";

    // ---------------------------------------------------------------- reading

    // Why a region was refused, and the node the refusal is about.
    //
    // A refusal carries a node rather than a place: the compiler reads the
    // range off the node, and an adapter has no operation for reading one.
    data Refusal {
        NoRefusal,
        Refused(node: Syntax, why: Text),
    }

    // The first refusal of two, in the order they were written.
    fn first_refusal(found: Refusal, later: Refusal) -> Refusal {
        match found {
            Refused(node, why) -> Refused(node, why),
            NoRefusal -> later,
        }
    }

    // What sounds first in a stretch of notation, by the spelling the composer
    // wrote for it.
    //
    // A tie reaches whatever sounds next, and "next" is usually in the next
    // bar. Reading from the end means the answer is already in hand when the
    // tie is met.
    data Sound {
        Silent,
        Sounds(spelling: Text, node: Syntax),
    }

    // A tie left hanging at the end of a stretch: it continues into whatever
    // follows the stretch, which the stretch itself cannot see.
    data Hanging {
        Closed,
        Hangs(spelling: Text, node: Syntax),
    }

    // One header field, once it has been read.
    data Given {
        Absent,
        Stated(node: Syntax),
    }

    // The six things a staff says about itself before any notation.
    data Head {
        Head(
            instrument: Given,
            shift: Given,
            written_clef: Given,
            tonality: Given,
            beats: Given,
            spelled: Given,
        ),
    }

    // What one stretch of notation reads to.
    data Reading {
        Reading(
            items: Syntax,
            span: Ratio,
            opens: Sound,
            hangs: Hanging,
            head: Head,
            refusal: Refusal,
        ),
    }

    // How many dots a written value carries.
    //
    // Four values and not a `Nat`, because the count has to be emitted as a
    // numeral and this adapter can only emit numerals it can spell.
    data Dots {
        NoDots,
        OneDot,
        TwoDots,
        ThreeDots,
    }

    // One more dot, or nothing further.
    fn one_more_dot(sofar: Dots) -> Option<Dots> {
        match sofar {
            NoDots -> Some(OneDot),
            OneDot -> Some(TwoDots),
            TwoDots -> Some(ThreeDots),
            ThreeDots -> None,
        }
    }

    // What the dots multiply the undotted value by: each dot adds half of what
    // the dot before it added.
    fn dotted_factor(dots: Dots) -> Ratio {
        match dots {
            NoDots -> 1,
            OneDot -> 3/2,
            TwoDots -> 7/4,
            ThreeDots -> 15/8,
        }
    }

    // The written value a note or rest states, waiting for what it belongs to.
    data Length {
        NoLength,
        Divided(numeral: Syntax, dots: Dots, span: Ratio),
        Spanned(numeral: Syntax, span: Ratio),
    }

    // Whether what is being read is tied on to whatever sounds next.
    data Tying {
        Untied,
        Tied(node: Syntax),
    }

    // Up to two numbers a form stated in its parentheses.
    data Numbers {
        NoNumbers,
        OneNumber(first: Syntax, value: Ratio),
        TwoNumbers(first: Syntax, value: Ratio, second: Syntax, other: Ratio),
    }

    // A braces body a form has taken but not yet used.
    data Taken {
        NoBody,
        Took(spot: NodePath, read: Reading),
    }

    // The pitches of a chord or a grace group, waiting for what holds them.
    data Voiced {
        NoVoices,
        Voices(node: Syntax, spelling: Text, listed: Syntax),
    }

    // One word or literal, waiting for the word that says what it was.
    data Said {
        Said(spot: NodePath, kind: Text, spelling: Text),
    }

    // Up to two of them: `key d major` is the only form that takes two.
    data Words {
        NoWords,
        OneWord(only: Said),
        TwoWords(first: Said, second: Said),
    }

    // What has been read since the last word, reading from the end.
    //
    // This is the whole of the reader's state, and it is small on purpose:
    // every form in this notation is a word followed by its arguments, so
    // reading from the end means collecting the arguments and then meeting the
    // word that says what they were.
    data Pending {
        Pending(
            read: Reading,
            length: Length,
            dots: Dots,
            tying: Tying,
            numbers: Numbers,
            taken: Taken,
            voiced: Voiced,
            words: Words,
        ),
    }

    // One piece of a region, as the first pass tags it.
    //
    // A braces group is already a `Reading`, because the fold runs from the
    // leaves up: by the time a body's word is met, the body has been read.
    data Read {
        Trivia,
        Piece(spot: NodePath, kind: Text, spelling: Text),
        Grouped(spot: NodePath, delimiter: Text, parts: List<Read>),
        Body(spot: NodePath, read: Reading),
        Unreadable(spot: NodePath),
    }

    // --------------------------------------------------------------- emitting

    // Nothing said yet.
    let no_head = Head(Absent, Absent, Absent, Absent, Absent, Absent);

    // A name, as an expression.
    fn named(here: NodePath, role: Nat, spelling: Text) -> Syntax {
        syntax_identifier(syntax_built(here, role, 1), spelling)
    }

    // `name(one)`, `name(one, two)`, and so on. A call is a name beside its
    // parenthesised arguments, which is what the ordinary parser reads back.
    fn call1(here: NodePath, role: Nat, spelling: Text, one: Syntax) -> Syntax {
        syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 0), "layout", [
            named(here, role, spelling),
            syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 2), "parentheses", [one]),
        ])
    }

    fn call2(here: NodePath, role: Nat, spelling: Text, one: Syntax, two: Syntax) -> Syntax {
        syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 0), "layout", [
            named(here, role, spelling),
            syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 2), "parentheses", [
                one,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 3), "Comma", ","),
                two,
            ]),
        ])
    }

    fn call3(
        here: NodePath,
        role: Nat,
        spelling: Text,
        one: Syntax,
        two: Syntax,
        three: Syntax
    ) -> Syntax {
        syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 0), "layout", [
            named(here, role, spelling),
            syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 2), "parentheses", [
                one,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 3), "Comma", ","),
                two,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 4), "Comma", ","),
                three,
            ]),
        ])
    }

    fn call4(
        here: NodePath,
        role: Nat,
        spelling: Text,
        one: Syntax,
        two: Syntax,
        three: Syntax,
        four: Syntax,
    ) -> Syntax {
        syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 0), "layout", [
            named(here, role, spelling),
            syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 2), "parentheses", [
                one,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 3), "Comma", ","),
                two,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 4), "Comma", ","),
                three,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 5), "Comma", ","),
                four,
            ]),
        ])
    }

    fn call5(
        here: NodePath,
        role: Nat,
        spelling: Text,
        one: Syntax,
        two: Syntax,
        three: Syntax,
        four: Syntax,
        five: Syntax,
    ) -> Syntax {
        syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 0), "layout", [
            named(here, role, spelling),
            syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 2), "parentheses", [
                one,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 3), "Comma", ","),
                two,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 4), "Comma", ","),
                three,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 5), "Comma", ","),
                four,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 6), "Comma", ","),
                five,
            ]),
        ])
    }

    fn call7(
        here: NodePath,
        role: Nat,
        spelling: Text,
        one: Syntax,
        two: Syntax,
        three: Syntax,
        four: Syntax,
        five: Syntax,
        six: Syntax,
        seven: Syntax,
    ) -> Syntax {
        syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 0), "layout", [
            named(here, role, spelling),
            syntax_group(syntax_built(here, role, 2), "parentheses", [
                one,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 3), "Comma", ","),
                two,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 4), "Comma", ","),
                three,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 5), "Comma", ","),
                four,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 6), "Comma", ","),
                five,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 7), "Comma", ","),
                six,
                syntax_token(syntax_built(here, role, 8), "Comma", ","),
                seven,
            ]),
        ])
    }

    // The end of a written sequence.
    fn no_items(here: NodePath) -> Syntax {
        syntax_identifier(syntax_built(here, 31, 0), "NoItems")
    }

    // Nothing read at all.
    fn nothing_read(here: NodePath) -> Reading {
        Reading(no_items(here), 0, Silent, Closed, no_head, NoRefusal)
    }

    // The anchor of the node at `here`, or a zero where the compiler has no
    // range. An anchor is a number whose meaning is the compiler's table: this
    // adapter hands one over and can read nothing from it.
    fn anchored(region: Syntax, here: NodePath) -> Syntax {
        option_fold(
            syntax_token(syntax_built(here, 32, 0), "Integer", "0"),
            fn (node: Syntax) -> Syntax { node },
            syntax_anchor(region, here, syntax_built(here, 33, 0)),
        )
    }

    // `Tie`, as the package spells it.
    fn tie_of(here: NodePath, tying: Tying) -> Syntax {
        syntax_identifier(
            syntax_built(here, 34, 0),
            match tying {
                Untied -> "Untied",
                Tied(node) -> "TiedOn",
            },
        )
    }

    // `WrittenDuration`, as the package spells it.
    fn written_duration(here: NodePath, length: Length) -> Option<Syntax> {
        match length {
            NoLength -> None,
            Divided(numeral, dots, span) -> Some(call2(
                here,
                35,
                "NoteValue",
                numeral,
                syntax_token(
                    syntax_built(here, 30, 0),
                    "Integer",
                    match dots {
                        NoDots -> "0",
                        OneDot -> "1",
                        TwoDots -> "2",
                        ThreeDots -> "3",
                    },
                )
            )),
            Spanned(numeral, span) -> Some(call1(here, 36, "ExactSpan", numeral)),
        }
    }

    // The exact span a stated written value covers.
    fn stated_span(length: Length) -> Option<Ratio> {
        match length {
            NoLength -> None,
            Divided(numeral, dots, span) -> Some(span),
            Spanned(numeral, span) -> Some(span),
        }
    }

    // `Beats(count, unit)`, from the two numbers a form stated.
    fn beats_of(here: NodePath, numbers: Numbers) -> Option<Syntax> {
        match numbers {
            NoNumbers -> None,
            OneNumber(first, value) -> None,
            TwoNumbers(first, value, second, other) -> Some(call2(
                here,
                37,
                "Beats",
                first,
                second
            )),
        }
    }

    // What a stated meter measures, in whole notes.
    fn beats_span(numbers: Numbers) -> Option<Ratio> {
        match numbers {
            NoNumbers -> None,
            OneNumber(first, value) -> None,
            TwoNumbers(first, count, second, unit) -> match ratio_div(count, unit) {
                Ok(span) -> Some(span),
                Err(why) -> None,
            },
        }
    }

    // ---------------------------------------------------------------- pieces

    // The node the region holds at a path, for a refusal to point at. The
    // region itself stands in where there is nothing there, which cannot
    // happen for a path the fold handed out.
    fn node_at(region: Syntax, spot: NodePath) -> Syntax {
        option_fold(region, fn (node: Syntax) -> Syntax { node }, syntax_at(region, spot))
    }

    // Whether a piece is a written pitch.
    fn is_pitch(one: Read) -> Bool {
        match one {
            Piece(spot, kind, spelling) -> text_equal(kind, "PitchLiteral"),
            Trivia -> false,
            Grouped(spot, delimiter, parts) -> false,
            Body(spot, read) -> false,
            Unreadable(spot) -> false,
        }
    }

    // One pitch of a chord, written back with the comma that separates it from
    // the next. A layout group is transparent to the parser, so a list of them
    // reads as the list literal it spells.
    fn voice_written(here: NodePath, one: Read) -> Syntax {
        match one {
            Piece(spot, kind, spelling) -> syntax_group(syntax_built(spot, 42, 0), "layout", [
                syntax_token(syntax_built(spot, 41, 0), "PitchLiteral", spelling),
                syntax_token(syntax_built(spot, 43, 0), "Comma", ","),
            ]),
            Trivia -> syntax_token(syntax_built(here, 44, 0), "Missing", ""),
            Grouped(spot, delimiter, parts) -> syntax_token(
                syntax_built(here, 44, 1),
                "Missing",
                ""
            ),
            Body(spot, read) -> syntax_token(syntax_built(here, 44, 2), "Missing", ""),
            Unreadable(spot) -> syntax_token(syntax_built(here, 44, 3), "Missing", ""),
        }
    }

    // The spelling of the first pitch among some pieces, if there is one.
    fn first_voice(parts: List<Read>) -> Option<Text> {
        list_fold_from_start(
            None,
            fn (one: Read, sofar: Option<Text>) -> Option<Text> {
                match sofar {
                    Some(found) -> Some(found),
                    None -> match one {
                        Piece(spot, kind, spelling) -> if text_equal(kind, "PitchLiteral") {
                            Some(spelling)
                        } else { None },
                        Trivia -> None,
                        Grouped(spot, delimiter, parts_inside) -> None,
                        Body(spot, read) -> None,
                        Unreadable(spot) -> None,
                    },
                }
            },
            parts,
        )
    }

    // The numbers a form stated between its parentheses, in the order written.
    fn stated_numbers(region: Syntax, parts: List<Read>) -> Numbers {
        list_fold_from_start(
            NoNumbers,
            fn (one: Read, sofar: Numbers) -> Numbers {
                match one {
                    Piece(spot, kind, spelling) -> match text_equal(kind, "Integer") {
                        true -> option_fold(
                            sofar,
                            fn (value: Ratio) -> Numbers {
                                match sofar {
                                    NoNumbers -> OneNumber(
                                        syntax_token(
                                            syntax_built(spot, 45, 0),
                                            "Integer",
                                            spelling
                                        ),
                                        value,
                                    ),
                                    OneNumber(first, already) -> TwoNumbers(
                                        first,
                                        already,
                                        syntax_token(
                                            syntax_built(spot, 45, 0),
                                            "Integer",
                                            spelling
                                        ),
                                        value,
                                    ),
                                    TwoNumbers(first, already, second, other) -> TwoNumbers(
                                        first,
                                        already,
                                        second,
                                        other,
                                    ),
                                }
                            },
                            syntax_number(node_at(region, spot)),
                        ),
                        false -> sofar,
                    },
                    Trivia -> sofar,
                    Grouped(spot, delimiter, inside) -> sofar,
                    Body(spot, read) -> sofar,
                    Unreadable(spot) -> sofar,
                }
            },
            parts,
        )
    }

    // The exact span a `( 3/8 )` states, if that is what the parentheses hold.
    fn stated_exact(region: Syntax, parts: List<Read>) -> Option<Length> {
        list_fold_from_start(
            None,
            fn (one: Read, sofar: Option<Length>) -> Option<Length> {
                match sofar {
                    Some(found) -> Some(found),
                    None -> match one {
                        Piece(spot, kind, spelling) -> match text_equal(kind, "Rational") {
                            true -> option_fold(
                                None,
                                fn (value: Ratio) -> Option<Length> {
                                    Some(Spanned(
                                        syntax_token(
                                            syntax_built(spot, 46, 0),
                                            "Rational",
                                            spelling
                                        ),
                                        value
                                    ))
                                },
                                syntax_number(node_at(region, spot)),
                            ),
                            false -> None,
                        },
                        Trivia -> None,
                        Grouped(spot, delimiter, inside) -> None,
                        Body(spot, read) -> None,
                        Unreadable(spot) -> None,
                    },
                }
            },
            parts,
        )
    }

    // The pitches of `[ … ]`, as the list expression the package's `Chord` and
    // `Grace` take, together with the first of them for a tie to meet.
    fn voiced_of(here: NodePath, parts: List<Read>) -> Voiced {
        option_fold(
            NoVoices,
            fn (spelling: Text) -> Voiced {
                Voices(
                    syntax_group(
                        syntax_built(here, 47, 0),
                        "brackets",
                        map(
                            fn (one: Read) -> Syntax { voice_written(here, one) },
                            filter(is_pitch, parts)
                        )
                    ),
                    spelling,
                    syntax_group(
                        syntax_built(here, 48, 0),
                        "brackets",
                        map(
                            fn (one: Read) -> Syntax { voice_written(here, one) },
                            filter(is_pitch, parts)
                        )
                    ),
                )
            },
            first_voice(parts),
        )
    }

    // ---------------------------------------------------------------- placing

    // What a form leaves behind: everything it took is used up, what follows
    // it is unchanged, and the sequence has grown by one item.
    fn after_item(
        later: Pending,
        items: Syntax,
        added: Ratio,
        opens: Sound,
        hangs: Hanging,
        trouble: Refusal,
    ) -> Pending {
        match later {
            Pending(read, length, dots, tying, numbers, taken, voiced, words) -> match read {
                Reading(was, span, was_open, was_hanging, head, refusal) -> Pending(
                    Reading(
                        items,
                        match ratio_add(span, added) {
                            Ok(total) -> total,
                            Err(why) -> span,
                        },
                        opens,
                        hangs,
                        head,
                        first_refusal(trouble, refusal),
                    ),
                    NoLength,
                    NoDots,
                    Untied,
                    NoNumbers,
                    NoBody,
                    NoVoices,
                    NoWords,
                ),
            },
        }
    }

    // A tie left open by what is being placed, met against what follows it.
    //
    // The tie is checked by spelling because a spelling is what the composer
    // wrote and all this adapter can see: `f5` tied to `f#5` is two different
    // texts, which is exactly the mistake worth catching.
    fn tie_met(hangs: Hanging, next: Sound, beyond: Hanging) -> Result<Hanging, Refusal> {
        match hangs {
            Closed -> Ok(beyond),
            Hangs(spelling, node) -> match next {
                Silent -> Ok(Hangs(spelling, node)),
                Sounds(other, at_node) -> if text_equal(spelling, other) {
                    Ok(beyond)
                } else {
                    Err(Refused(at_node, "this staff ties a note to a differently spelled one"))
                },
            },
        }
    }

    // Everything a placed item needs to know about what follows it.
    fn following(later: Pending) -> Reading {
        match later {
            Pending(read, length, dots, tying, numbers, taken, voiced, words) -> read,
        }
    }

    // One sounding item — a note, a rest, a chord, a grace group, a meter
    // change — placed in front of what follows it.
    fn sounding(
        region: Syntax,
        here: NodePath,
        later: Pending,
        event: Syntax,
        added: Ratio,
        opens: Sound,
        hangs: Hanging,
    ) -> Pending {
        match following(later) {
            Reading(items, span, next, beyond, head, refusal) -> match tie_met(
                hangs,
                next,
                beyond
            ) {
                Ok(reached) -> after_item(
                    later,
                    call3(here, 1, "Sounded", anchored(region, here), event, items),
                    added,
                    match opens {
                        Silent -> next,
                        Sounds(spelling, node) -> Sounds(spelling, node),
                    },
                    reached,
                    NoRefusal,
                ),
                Err(why) -> after_item(later, items, added, next, beyond, why),
            },
        }
    }

    // A nested form — a bar, a slur, a tuplet, a repeat, an ending — placed in
    // front of what follows it, carrying its body's own reading with it.
    //
    // What went wrong inside is reported before what went wrong around it: a
    // bar whose notation the reader could not read does not measure what it
    // says either, and that second sentence is a consequence of the first
    // rather than a second fault.
    fn nesting(
        here: NodePath,
        later: Pending,
        built: Syntax,
        body: Reading,
        added: Ratio,
        trouble: Refusal,
    ) -> Pending {
        match body {
            Reading(inner, inner_span, inner_opens, inner_hangs, inner_head, inner_refusal) -> match following(
                later,
            ) {
                Reading(items, span, next, beyond, head, refusal) -> match tie_met(
                    inner_hangs,
                    next,
                    beyond,
                ) {
                    Ok(reached) -> after_item(
                        later,
                        built,
                        added,
                        match inner_opens {
                            Silent -> next,
                            Sounds(spelling, node) -> Sounds(spelling, node),
                        },
                        reached,
                        first_refusal(inner_refusal, trouble),
                    ),
                    Err(why) -> after_item(
                        later,
                        items,
                        added,
                        next,
                        beyond,
                        first_refusal(trouble, first_refusal(inner_refusal, why)),
                    ),
                },
            },
        }
    }

    // A refusal that leaves what is being read where it is.
    //
    // `refusing` ends the item it is reading, which is right when the item is
    // the fault. A fault found while a written value is still in hand is not:
    // clearing it would make the note that value belongs to look valueless,
    // and the reader would go on to say so — a second sentence about a note
    // that is not what went wrong.
    fn faulting(later: Pending, node: Syntax, why: Text) -> Pending {
        match later {
            Pending(read, length, dots, tying, numbers, taken, voiced, words) -> match read {
                Reading(items, span, opens, hangs, head, refusal) -> Pending(
                    Reading(
                        items,
                        span,
                        opens,
                        hangs,
                        head,
                        first_refusal(Refused(node, why), refusal),
                    ),
                    length,
                    dots,
                    tying,
                    numbers,
                    taken,
                    voiced,
                    words,
                ),
            },
        }
    }

    // A refusal, with nothing placed.
    fn refusing(later: Pending, node: Syntax, why: Text) -> Pending {
        match following(later) {
            Reading(items, span, next, beyond, head, refusal) -> after_item(
                later,
                items,
                0,
                next,
                beyond,
                Refused(node, why),
            ),
        }
    }

    // ----------------------------------------------------------- what is held

    // The written value the next note takes, or the refusal that says it was
    // stated twice.
    //
    // A value is spent the moment the note it belongs to is read, so a value
    // arriving while one is already held belongs to no note that has been
    // read: `c5/4/8` states two, and neither of them is more the note's than
    // the other.
    fn holding_length(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        later: Pending,
        length: Length
    ) -> Pending {
        match later {
            Pending(r, was, dots, tying, numbers, taken, voiced, words) -> match was {
                // The left `length` is the field; the right is this
                // function's parameter. A right-hand side reads the scope
                // around the update, never the fields of its subject.
                NoLength -> later with {
                    length = length,
                    dots = NoDots
                },
                Divided(numeral, held_dots, span) -> faulting(
                    later,
                    node_at(region, spot),
                    "this note states two written values",
                ),
                Spanned(numeral, span) -> faulting(
                    later,
                    node_at(region, spot),
                    "this note states two written values",
                ),
            },
        }
    }

    // One more word waiting for the word that says what it was. A third is one
    // more than any form in this notation takes.
    fn holding_word(region: Syntax, later: Pending, said: Said) -> Pending {
        match later {
            Pending(r, length, dots, tying, numbers, taken, voiced, words) -> match words {
                NoWords -> later with {
                    words = OneWord(said)
                },
                OneWord(only) -> later with {
                    words = TwoWords(said, only)
                },
                TwoWords(first, second) -> match said {
                    Said(spot, kind, spelling) -> refusing(
                        later,
                        node_at(region, spot),
                        "this staff does not know this word",
                    ),
                },
            },
        }
    }

    // The head this reading states, with one more field filled in, or the
    // refusal that says it was stated twice.
    //
    // Five words, and a head holds one of each. A sixth statement of the same
    // word is not a correction: nothing here is written in order, so the
    // reader has no way to say which of the two the composer meant.
    fn stating(head: Head, which: Text, given: Syntax, node: Syntax) -> Result<Head, Refusal> {
        match head {
            Head(instrument, shift, written_clef, tonality, beats, spelled) -> match which {
                "instrument" -> match instrument {
                    Absent -> Ok(Head(
                        Stated(given),
                        shift,
                        written_clef,
                        tonality,
                        beats,
                        spelled
                    )),
                    Stated(already) -> Err(Refused(node, "this staff says this twice")),
                },
                "transposing" -> match shift {
                    Absent -> Ok(Head(
                        instrument,
                        Stated(given),
                        written_clef,
                        tonality,
                        beats,
                        spelled
                    )),
                    Stated(already) -> Err(Refused(node, "this staff says this twice")),
                },
                "clef" -> match written_clef {
                    Absent -> Ok(Head(
                        instrument,
                        shift,
                        Stated(given),
                        tonality,
                        beats,
                        spelled
                    )),
                    Stated(already) -> Err(Refused(node, "this staff says this twice")),
                },
                "key" -> match tonality {
                    Absent -> Ok(Head(
                        instrument,
                        shift,
                        written_clef,
                        Stated(given),
                        beats,
                        spelled
                    )),
                    Stated(already) -> Err(Refused(node, "this staff says this twice")),
                },
                "time" -> match beats {
                    Absent -> Ok(Head(
                        instrument,
                        shift,
                        written_clef,
                        tonality,
                        Stated(given),
                        spelled
                    )),
                    Stated(already) -> Err(Refused(node, "this staff says this twice")),
                },
                _ -> match spelled {
                    Absent -> Ok(Head(
                        instrument,
                        shift,
                        written_clef,
                        tonality,
                        beats,
                        Stated(given)
                    )),
                    Stated(already) -> Err(Refused(node, "this staff says this twice")),
                },
            },
        }
    }

    // A header field, read and put away. Nothing is placed: a header is what
    // the staff is, not something on it.
    fn heading(later: Pending, which: Text, given: Syntax, node: Syntax) -> Pending {
        match later {
            Pending(read, length, dots, tying, numbers, taken, voiced, words) -> match read {
                Reading(items, span, opens, hangs, head, refusal) -> match stating(
                    head,
                    which,
                    given,
                    node,
                ) {
                    Ok(stated) -> Pending(
                        Reading(items, span, opens, hangs, stated, refusal),
                        NoLength,
                        NoDots,
                        Untied,
                        NoNumbers,
                        NoBody,
                        NoVoices,
                        NoWords,
                    ),
                    Err(why) -> Pending(
                        Reading(items, span, opens, hangs, head, first_refusal(why, refusal)),
                        NoLength,
                        NoDots,
                        Untied,
                        NoNumbers,
                        NoBody,
                        NoVoices,
                        NoWords,
                    ),
                },
            },
        }
    }

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ the forms

    // What a clef word names.
    fn clef_named(here: NodePath, spelling: Text) -> Option<Syntax> {
        if text_equal(spelling, "treble") {
            Some(syntax_identifier(syntax_built(here, 38, 0), "Treble"))
        } else if text_equal(spelling, "bass") {
            Some(syntax_identifier(syntax_built(here, 38, 1), "Bass"))
        } else if text_equal(spelling, "alto") {
            Some(syntax_identifier(syntax_built(here, 38, 2), "Alto"))
        } else if text_equal(spelling, "tenor") {
            Some(syntax_identifier(syntax_built(here, 38, 3), "Tenor"))
        } else { None }
    }

    // What a spelling word names.
    fn spelling_named(here: NodePath, spelling: Text) -> Option<Syntax> {
        if text_equal(spelling, "shortest_readable") {
            Some(syntax_identifier(syntax_built(here, 39, 0), "ShortestReadable"))
        } else if text_equal(spelling, "exact_values") {
            Some(syntax_identifier(syntax_built(here, 39, 1), "ExactValues"))
        } else { None }
    }

    // `rest/8` — a written silence.
    fn rest_read(region: Syntax, spot: NodePath, later: Pending, length: Length) -> Pending {
        match written_duration(spot, length) {
            None -> refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this rest states no written value"),
            Some(value) -> option_fold(
                refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this rest states no written value"),
                fn (span: Ratio) -> Pending {
                    sounding(
                        region,
                        spot,
                        later,
                        call1(spot, 3, "Rest", value),
                        span,
                        Silent,
                        Closed,
                    )
                },
                stated_span(length),
            ),
        }
    }

    // `c5/4`, `d5/4.`, `f5/4 ~`, `c5(3/8)` — one written note.
    fn note_read(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        later: Pending,
        spelling: Text,
        length: Length,
        tying: Tying,
    ) -> Pending {
        match written_duration(spot, length) {
            None -> refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this note states no written value"),
            Some(value) -> option_fold(
                refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this note states no written value"),
                fn (span: Ratio) -> Pending {
                    sounding(
                        region,
                        spot,
                        later,
                        call3(
                            spot,
                            2,
                            "Note",
                            syntax_token(syntax_built(spot, 49, 0), "PitchLiteral", spelling),
                            value,
                            tie_of(spot, tying),
                        ),
                        span,
                        Sounds(spelling, node_at(region, spot)),
                        match tying {
                            Untied -> Closed,
                            Tied(node) -> Hangs(spelling, node),
                        },
                    )
                },
                stated_span(length),
            ),
        }
    }

    // `[g4 b4 d5]/4` — one written chord.
    fn chord_read(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        later: Pending,
        voiced: Voiced,
        length: Length,
        tying: Tying,
    ) -> Pending {
        match voiced {
            NoVoices -> refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this chord holds no pitches"),
            Voices(node, spelling, listed) -> match written_duration(spot, length) {
                None -> refusing(
                    later,
                    node_at(region, spot),
                    "this chord states no written value"
                ),
                Some(value) -> option_fold(
                    refusing(
                        later,
                        node_at(region, spot),
                        "this chord states no written value"
                    ),
                    fn (span: Ratio) -> Pending {
                        sounding(
                            region,
                            spot,
                            later,
                            call3(spot, 4, "Chord", listed, value, tie_of(spot, tying)),
                            span,
                            Sounds(spelling, node_at(region, spot)),
                            match tying {
                                Untied -> Closed,
                                Tied(hung) -> Hangs(spelling, hung),
                            },
                        )
                    },
                    stated_span(length),
                ),
            },
        }
    }

    // What follows the item being placed.
    fn after_items(later: Pending) -> Syntax {
        match following(later) {
            Reading(items, span, opens, hangs, head, refusal) -> items,
        }
    }

    // What a body reads to, or nothing read at all.
    fn body_of(here: NodePath, taken: Taken) -> Reading {
        match taken {
            NoBody -> nothing_read(here),
            Took(spot, read) -> read,
        }
    }

    // `bar (4, 4) { … }` and `pickup (1, 4) { … }` — a measure of stated
    // length, checked against what it holds.
    //
    // This is one of the two diagnostics the trial note asks for, and it lands
    // on the bar the composer wrote because the adapter is the one holding a
    // node. The package could find the same fault and could not point at it.
    fn bar_read(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        later: Pending,
        numbers: Numbers,
        taken: Taken
    ) -> Pending {
        match taken {
            NoBody -> refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this bar holds no notation"),
            Took(body_at, body) -> option_fold(
                refusing(
                    later,
                    node_at(region, spot),
                    "this bar does not say what it measures"
                ),
                fn (wanted: Ratio) -> Pending {
                    option_fold(
                        refusing(
                            later,
                            node_at(region, spot),
                            "this bar does not say what it measures"
                        ),
                        fn (beats: Syntax) -> Pending {
                            match body {
                                Reading(items, span, opens, hangs, head, refusal) -> nesting(
                                    spot,
                                    later,
                                    call4(
                                        spot,
                                        7,
                                        "Bar",
                                        anchored(region, spot),
                                        beats,
                                        items,
                                        after_items(later),
                                    ),
                                    body,
                                    wanted,
                                    if ratio_equal(span, wanted) {
                                        NoRefusal
                                    } else {
                                        Refused(
                                            node_at(region, spot),
                                            "this bar does not hold what it says it measures",
                                        )
                                    },
                                ),
                            }
                        },
                        beats_of(spot, numbers),
                    )
                },
                beats_span(numbers),
            ),
        }
    }

    // `slur { … }` — one phrase mark over what it holds.
    fn slur_read(region: Syntax, spot: NodePath, later: Pending, taken: Taken) -> Pending {
        match taken {
            NoBody -> refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this slur holds no notation"),
            Took(body_at, body) -> match body {
                Reading(items, span, opens, hangs, head, refusal) -> nesting(
                    spot,
                    later,
                    call3(spot, 8, "Slur", anchored(region, spot), items, after_items(later)),
                    body,
                    span,
                    NoRefusal,
                ),
            },
        }
    }

    // `tuplet (3, 2) { … }` — three in the time of two, and the bracket is
    // kept rather than resolved: what the notes become is `realize`'s answer.
    fn tuplet_read(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        later: Pending,
        numbers: Numbers,
        taken: Taken,
    ) -> Pending {
        match taken {
            NoBody -> refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this tuplet holds no notation"),
            Took(body_at, body) -> match numbers {
                NoNumbers -> refusing(
                    later,
                    node_at(region, spot),
                    "this tuplet states no ratio"
                ),
                OneNumber(first, value) -> refusing(
                    later,
                    node_at(region, spot),
                    "this tuplet states no ratio",
                ),
                TwoNumbers(first, played, second, against) -> match ratio_equal(played, 0) {
                    true -> refusing(
                        later,
                        node_at(region, spot),
                        "this tuplet plays no notes in the time of some",
                    ),
                    false -> match body {
                        Reading(items, span, opens, hangs, head, refusal) -> nesting(
                            spot,
                            later,
                            call5(
                                spot,
                                9,
                                "Tuplet",
                                anchored(region, spot),
                                first,
                                second,
                                items,
                                after_items(later),
                            ),
                            body,
                            match ratio_div(against, played) {
                                Ok(factor) -> match ratio_mul(span, factor) {
                                    Ok(outside) -> outside,
                                    Err(why) -> span,
                                },
                                Err(why) -> span,
                            },
                            NoRefusal,
                        ),
                    },
                },
            },
        }
    }

    // `repeat (2) { … }` and `ending (1) { … }`.
    //
    // Written time counts the page and not the performance, so a repeat covers
    // its body once: how many times it sounds is a reading of the score.
    fn repeated_read(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        later: Pending,
        role: Nat,
        spelling: Text,
        numbers: Numbers,
        taken: Taken,
        missing: Text,
    ) -> Pending {
        match taken {
            NoBody -> refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), missing),
            Took(body_at, body) -> match numbers {
                NoNumbers -> refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), missing),
                OneNumber(first, value) -> match body {
                    Reading(items, span, opens, hangs, head, refusal) -> nesting(
                        spot,
                        later,
                        call4(
                            spot,
                            role,
                            spelling,
                            anchored(region, spot),
                            first,
                            items,
                            after_items(later)
                        ),
                        body,
                        span,
                        NoRefusal,
                    ),
                },
                TwoNumbers(first, value, second, other) -> refusing(
                    later,
                    node_at(region, spot),
                    missing
                ),
            },
        }
    }

    // `time (4, 4)` — the meter this staff opens in.
    //
    // A different word from the `meter (3, 4)` that changes it, and the region
    // grouper is the reason. An adapter cannot see lines, so it cannot tell a
    // word written above the music from the same word written among it; two
    // words is what that costs. The notation carries the cost well enough — a
    // staff opens in a time signature and changes meter later — and the head
    // reads like the five statements beside it rather than like an item.
    fn time_header(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        later: Pending,
        numbers: Numbers
    ) -> Pending {
        option_fold(
            refusing(
                later,
                node_at(region, spot),
                "this staff does not say what time it opens in"
            ),
            fn (beats: Syntax) -> Pending {
                heading(later, "time", beats, node_at(region, spot))
            },
            beats_of(spot, numbers),
        )
    }

    // `meter (3, 4)` — the meter changes here, and the bars after it say so
    // themselves.
    fn meter_read(region: Syntax, spot: NodePath, later: Pending, numbers: Numbers) -> Pending {
        option_fold(
            refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this meter states no count and unit"),
            fn (beats: Syntax) -> Pending {
                sounding(
                    region,
                    spot,
                    later,
                    call1(spot, 6, "MeterChange", beats),
                    0,
                    Silent,
                    Closed,
                )
            },
            beats_of(spot, numbers),
        )
    }

    // `grace [e5]` — written pitches with no written duration. What a grace
    // takes, and what it takes it from, is a performance profile's choice.
    fn grace_read(region: Syntax, spot: NodePath, later: Pending, voiced: Voiced) -> Pending {
        match voiced {
            NoVoices -> refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this grace holds no pitches"),
            Voices(node, spelling, listed) -> sounding(
                region,
                spot,
                later,
                call1(spot, 5, "Grace", listed),
                0,
                Silent,
                Closed,
            ),
        }
    }

    // ------------------------------------------------------------- the header

    // The one word a header field took, if it took exactly one.
    fn only_word(words: Words) -> Option<Said> {
        match words {
            NoWords -> None,
            OneWord(only) -> Some(only),
            TwoWords(first, second) -> None,
        }
    }

    // Why a header field did not take exactly one word.
    //
    // No word at all is an empty field. Two words means one of them stands
    // between the field and its argument, and nothing in this staff reads a
    // word in that position — so the useful sentence names *that* word rather
    // than reporting the field as empty, which it is not. The reader works
    // from the end, so the field's own argument is the nearer of the two and
    // the stray one is the further.
    fn stray_word(region: Syntax, spot: NodePath, later: Pending, words: Words) -> Pending {
        match words {
            NoWords -> refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this staff field says nothing"),
            OneWord(only) -> refusing(
                later,
                node_at(region, spot),
                "this staff field says nothing"
            ),
            TwoWords(first, second) -> match second {
                Said(stray_at, stray_kind, spelling) -> refusing(
                    later,
                    node_at(region, stray_at),
                    "this staff does not know this word",
                ),
            },
        }
    }

    // `instrument "bb_clarinet"` and `transposing M2` — a literal written back
    // as the composer spelled it.
    fn literal_header(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        later: Pending,
        which: Text,
        kind: Text,
        words: Words,
    ) -> Pending {
        option_fold(
            stray_word(region, spot, later, words),
            fn (said: Said) -> Pending {
                match said {
                    Said(word_at, said_kind, spelling) -> if text_equal(said_kind, kind) {
                        heading(
                            later,
                            which,
                            syntax_token(syntax_built(word_at, 50, 0), kind, spelling),
                            node_at(region, word_at),
                        )
                    } else {
                        refusing(
                            later,
                            node_at(region, word_at),
                            "this staff field was given the wrong kind of word",
                        )
                    },
                }
            },
            only_word(words),
        )
    }

    // `clef treble` and `spelling shortest_readable` — a word this adapter
    // knows, or the refusal that says it does not.
    fn named_header(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        later: Pending,
        which: Text,
        words: Words,
    ) -> Pending {
        option_fold(
            stray_word(region, spot, later, words),
            fn (said: Said) -> Pending {
                match said {
                    Said(word_at, said_kind, spelling) -> option_fold(
                        refusing(
                            later,
                            node_at(region, word_at),
                            "this staff does not know this word",
                        ),
                        fn (given: Syntax) -> Pending {
                            heading(later, which, given, node_at(region, word_at))
                        },
                        if text_equal(which, "clef") {
                            clef_named(word_at, spelling)
                        } else { spelling_named(word_at, spelling) },
                    ),
                }
            },
            only_word(words),
        )
    }

    // `key d major` — written back as the key expression the composer wrote,
    // parenthesised so that it reads as one argument.
    fn key_header(region: Syntax, spot: NodePath, later: Pending, words: Words) -> Pending {
        match words {
            TwoWords(first, second) -> match first {
                Said(tonic_at, tonic_kind, tonic) -> match second {
                    Said(mode_at, mode_kind, mode) -> heading(
                        later,
                        "key",
                        syntax_group(syntax_built(spot, 51, 0), "parentheses", [
                            syntax_token(syntax_built(spot, 51, 1), "KeyKw", "key"),
                            syntax_token(syntax_built(tonic_at, 52, 0), "Identifier", tonic),
                            syntax_token(syntax_built(mode_at, 52, 1), "Identifier", mode),
                        ]),
                        node_at(region, spot),
                    ),
                },
            },
            NoWords -> refusing(
                later,
                node_at(region, spot),
                "this key names no tonic and no mode"
            ),
            OneWord(only) -> refusing(
                later,
                node_at(region, spot),
                "this key names no tonic and no mode"
            ),
        }
    }

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ the reader

    // One word, and what it does with whatever was read since the last one.
    //
    // Every word the staff spelling has, in one table. A word either opens a
    // form — a bar, a slur, a tuplet, a repeat — or states one of the six
    // facts a document carries in its head. Anything else is a word this staff
    // does not know, and is held rather than refused here, because what comes
    // after it is often what says which word it was meant to be.
    fn word_read(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        spelling: Text,
        kind: Text,
        later: Pending
    ) -> Pending {
        match later {
            Pending(read, length, dots, tying, numbers, taken, voiced, words) -> match spelling {
                "rest" -> rest_read(region, spot, later, length),
                "bar" -> bar_read(region, spot, later, numbers, taken),
                "pickup" -> bar_read(region, spot, later, numbers, taken),
                "slur" -> slur_read(region, spot, later, taken),
                "tuplet" -> tuplet_read(region, spot, later, numbers, taken),
                "grace" -> grace_read(region, spot, later, voiced),
                "repeat" -> repeated_read(
                    region,
                    spot,
                    later,
                    10,
                    "Repeat",
                    numbers,
                    taken,
                    "this repeat does not say how many times it holds what",
                ),
                "ending" -> repeated_read(
                    region,
                    spot,
                    later,
                    11,
                    "Ending",
                    numbers,
                    taken,
                    "this ending does not say which pass it holds what for",
                ),
                "time" -> time_header(region, spot, later, numbers),
                "meter" -> meter_read(region, spot, later, numbers),
                "instrument" -> literal_header(
                    region,
                    spot,
                    later,
                    "instrument",
                    "String",
                    words
                ),
                "transposing" -> literal_header(
                    region,
                    spot,
                    later,
                    "transposing",
                    "IntervalLiteral",
                    words
                ),
                "clef" -> named_header(region, spot, later, "clef", words),
                "spelling" -> named_header(region, spot, later, "spelling", words),
                "key" -> key_header(region, spot, later, words),
                _ -> holding_word(region, later, Said(spot, kind, spelling)),
            },
        }
    }

    // One token, by what the lexer called it.
    fn token_read(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        kind: Text,
        spelling: Text,
        later: Pending
    ) -> Pending {
        match later {
            Pending(read, length, dots, tying, numbers, taken, voiced, words) -> match kind {
                "Tilde" -> later with {
                    tying = Tied(node_at(region, spot))
                },
                "Dot" -> option_fold(
                    refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this value carries too many dots"),
                    fn (more: Dots) -> Pending { later with { dots = more } },
                    one_more_dot(dots),
                ),
                "Integer" -> option_fold(
                    refusing(later, node_at(region, spot), "this is not a written value"),
                    fn (value: Ratio) -> Pending {
                        match ratio_div(dotted_factor(dots), value) {
                            Ok(span) -> holding_length(
                                region,
                                spot,
                                later,
                                Divided(
                                    syntax_token(
                                        syntax_built(spot, 53, 0),
                                        "Integer",
                                        spelling
                                    ),
                                    dots,
                                    span,
                                ),
                            ),
                            Err(why) -> refusing(
                                later,
                                node_at(region, spot),
                                "this is not a written value",
                            ),
                        }
                    },
                    syntax_number(node_at(region, spot)),
                ),
                "PitchLiteral" -> note_read(region, spot, later, spelling, length, tying),
                "Slash" -> later,
                "Comma" -> later,
                _ -> word_read(region, spot, spelling, kind, later),
            },
        }
    }

    // One group: parentheses state numbers or an exact span, brackets hold
    // pitches, and braces have already been read.
    fn group_read(
        region: Syntax,
        spot: NodePath,
        delimiter: Text,
        parts: List<Read>,
        later: Pending,
    ) -> Pending {
        match later {
            Pending(read, length, dots, tying, numbers, taken, voiced, words) -> match delimiter {
                "parentheses" -> option_fold(
                    later with {
                        numbers = stated_numbers(region, parts)
                    },
                    fn (exact: Length) -> Pending { holding_length(region, spot, later, exact) },
                    stated_exact(region, parts),
                ),
                "brackets" -> match length {
                    NoLength -> later with {
                        voiced = voiced_of(spot, parts)
                    },
                    Divided(numeral, held_dots, span) -> chord_read(
                        region,
                        spot,
                        later,
                        voiced_of(spot, parts),
                        length,
                        tying,
                    ),
                    Spanned(numeral, span) -> chord_read(
                        region,
                        spot,
                        later,
                        voiced_of(spot, parts),
                        length,
                        tying,
                    ),
                },
                _ -> later,
            },
        }
    }

    // One piece of a region, read into what follows it.
    fn taken_piece(region: Syntax, one_piece: Read, later: Pending) -> Pending {
        match one_piece {
            Trivia -> later,
            Unreadable(spot) -> refusing(
                later,
                node_at(region, spot),
                "this staff cannot read this"
            ),
            Body(spot, read) -> later with {
                taken = Took(spot, read)
            },
            Grouped(spot, delimiter, parts) -> group_read(
                region,
                spot,
                delimiter,
                parts,
                later
            ),
            Piece(spot, kind, spelling) -> token_read(region, spot, kind, spelling, later),
        }
    }

    // Anything read and never used is something this staff did not understand.
    fn leftover(
        region: Syntax,
        here: NodePath,
        length: Length,
        numbers: Numbers,
        taken: Taken,
        voiced: Voiced,
        words: Words,
    ) -> Refusal {
        match words {
            OneWord(only) -> match only {
                Said(spot, kind, spelling) -> Refused(
                    node_at(region, spot),
                    "this staff does not know this word",
                ),
            },
            TwoWords(first, second) -> match first {
                Said(spot, kind, spelling) -> Refused(
                    node_at(region, spot),
                    "this staff does not know this word",
                ),
            },
            NoWords -> match voiced {
                Voices(node, spelling, listed) -> Refused(
                    node,
                    "these pitches are held for nothing"
                ),
                NoVoices -> match taken {
                    Took(spot, read) -> Refused(
                        node_at(region, spot),
                        "this staff does not know what holds this",
                    ),
                    NoBody -> match numbers {
                        OneNumber(first, value) -> Refused(
                            node_at(region, here),
                            "this staff does not know what these numbers are for",
                        ),
                        TwoNumbers(first, value, second, other) -> Refused(
                            node_at(region, here),
                            "this staff does not know what these numbers are for",
                        ),
                        NoNumbers -> match length {
                            Divided(numeral, dots, span) -> Refused(
                                node_at(region, here),
                                "this written value belongs to nothing",
                            ),
                            Spanned(numeral, span) -> Refused(
                                node_at(region, here),
                                "this written value belongs to nothing",
                            ),
                            NoLength -> NoRefusal,
                        },
                    },
                },
            },
        }
    }

    // Everything between one pair of braces, read.
    //
    // The fold runs from the end because the data this adapter emits is
    // right-nested: what a tie reaches is already in hand when the tie is met.
    fn read_body(region: Syntax, here: NodePath, pieces: List<Read>) -> Reading {
        match list_fold_from_end(
            Pending(
                nothing_read(here),
                NoLength,
                NoDots,
                Untied,
                NoNumbers,
                NoBody,
                NoVoices,
                NoWords,
            ),
            fn (one_piece: Read, later: Pending) -> Pending {
                taken_piece(region, one_piece, later)
            },
            pieces,
        ) {
            Pending(read, length, dots, tying, numbers, taken, voiced, words) -> match read {
                Reading(items, span, opens, hangs, head, refusal) -> Reading(
                    items,
                    span,
                    opens,
                    hangs,
                    head,
                    first_refusal(
                        leftover(region, here, length, numbers, taken, voiced, words),
                        refusal,
                    ),
                ),
            },
        }
    }

    // ---------------------------------------------------------- the document

    // A field the staff had to state.
    fn stated_field(
        region: Syntax,
        here: NodePath,
        field: Given,
        missing: Text
    ) -> Result<Syntax, Refusal> {
        match field {
            Absent -> Err(Refused(node_at(region, here), missing)),
            Stated(node) -> Ok(node),
        }
    }

    // The whole staff, as the one expression a region expands to.
    fn document_read(
        region: Syntax,
        here: NodePath,
        read: Reading
    ) -> Result<Syntax, (Syntax, Text)> {
        match read {
            Reading(items, span, opens, hangs, head, refusal) -> match refusal {
                Refused(node, why) -> Err((node, why)),
                NoRefusal -> match hangs {
                    Hangs(spelling, node) -> Err((
                        node,
                        "this staff ties a note to nothing: no note sounds after it"
                    )),
                    Closed -> match head {
                        Head(instrument, shift, written_clef, tonality, beats, spelled) -> match stated_field(
                            region,
                            here,
                            instrument,
                            "this staff does not say what instrument it is written for",
                        ) {
                            Err(why) -> match why {
                                Refused(node, told) -> Err((node, told)),
                                NoRefusal -> Err((
                                    node_at(region, here),
                                    "this staff is incomplete"
                                )),
                            },
                            Ok(named_instrument) -> match stated_field(
                                region,
                                here,
                                shift,
                                "this staff does not say how far its written pitch sits from its sounding pitch",
                            ) {
                                Err(why) -> match why {
                                    Refused(node, told) -> Err((node, told)),
                                    NoRefusal -> Err((
                                        node_at(region, here),
                                        "this staff is incomplete"
                                    )),
                                },
                                Ok(sounding_shift) -> match stated_field(
                                    region,
                                    here,
                                    written_clef,
                                    "this staff does not say what clef it is read in",
                                ) {
                                    Err(why) -> match why {
                                        Refused(node, told) -> Err((node, told)),
                                        NoRefusal -> Err((
                                            node_at(region, here),
                                            "this staff is incomplete"
                                        )),
                                    },
                                    Ok(read_clef) -> match stated_field(
                                        region,
                                        here,
                                        tonality,
                                        "this staff does not say what key it is written in",
                                    ) {
                                        Err(why) -> match why {
                                            Refused(node, told) -> Err((node, told)),
                                            NoRefusal -> Err((
                                                node_at(region, here),
                                                "this staff is incomplete"
                                            )),
                                        },
                                        Ok(written_key) -> match stated_field(
                                            region,
                                            here,
                                            beats,
                                            "this staff does not say what time it opens in",
                                        ) {
                                            Err(why) -> match why {
                                                Refused(node, told) -> Err((node, told)),
                                                NoRefusal -> Err((
                                                    node_at(region, here),
                                                    "this staff is incomplete"
                                                )),
                                            },
                                            Ok(opening) -> match stated_field(
                                                region,
                                                here,
                                                spelled,
                                                "this staff does not say how a realized span is spelled",
                                            ) {
                                                Err(why) -> match why {
                                                    Refused(node, told) -> Err((node, told)),
                                                    NoRefusal -> Err((
                                                        node_at(region, here),
                                                        "this staff is incomplete"
                                                    )),
                                                },
                                                Ok(spelling) -> Ok(call7(
                                                    here,
                                                    19,
                                                    "Document",
                                                    named_instrument,
                                                    sounding_shift,
                                                    read_clef,
                                                    written_key,
                                                    opening,
                                                    spelling,
                                                    items
                                                )),
                                            },
                                        },
                                    },
                                },
                            },
                        },
                    },
                },
            },
        }
    }

    // One region of staff notation, read into one ordinary expression.
    let expand = fn (region) {
        match syntax_fold(
            fn (here) { Unreadable(here) },
            fn (here, kind, text) {
                if text_equal(kind, "Whitespace") {
                    Trivia
                } else if text_equal(kind, "LineComment") {
                    Trivia
                } else if text_equal(kind, "BlockComment") {
                    Trivia
                } else { Piece(here, kind, text) }
            },
            fn (here, name) { Piece(here, "Identifier", name) },
            fn (here, delimiter, children) {
                if text_equal(delimiter, "braces") {
                    Body(here, read_body(region, here, children))
                } else { Grouped(here, delimiter, children) }
            },
            region,
        ) {
            Body(spot, read) -> document_read(region, spot, read),
            Trivia -> Err((region, "a staff region is written between braces")),
            Piece(spot, kind, spelling) -> Err((
                region,
                "a staff region is written between braces"
            )),
            Grouped(spot, delimiter, parts) -> Err((
                region,
                "a staff region is written between braces"
            )),
            Unreadable(spot) -> Err((region, "a staff region is written between braces")),
        }
    };
}
